\id ROM SAGE bounded evidence packet
\c 1
\v 1 Paul, a bond-servant of Christ Jesus, \f 1 \fr 1:1 \fr*\ft Lit \+it a called apostle\+it*\ft*\f*called \it as\it* an apostle, set apart for the gospel of God,
\v 2 which He promised beforehand through His prophets in the holy Scriptures,
\v 3 concerning His Son, who was born of a \f 1 \fr 1:3 \fr*\ft Lit \+it seed\+it*\ft*\f*descendant of David according to the flesh,
\v 4 who was declared the Son of God with power according to the \f 1 \fr 1:4 \fr*\ft Or \+it spirit\+it*\ft*\f*Spirit of holiness \f 2 \fr 1:4 \fr*\ft Or \+it as a result of\+it*\ft*\f*by the resurrection from the dead, Jesus Christ our Lord,
\v 5 through whom we have received grace and apostleship \f 1 \fr 1:5 \fr*\ft Lit \+it for obedience\+it*\ft*\f*to bring about \it the\it* obedience of faith among all the Gentiles in behalf of His name,
\v 6 among whom you also are \it the\it* called of Jesus Christ;
\v 7 to all who are beloved of God in Rome, called \it as\it* \f 1 \fr 1:7 \fr*\ft Lit \+it holy ones;\+it* i.e., God’s people\ft*\f*saints: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
\v 8 First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ \f 1 \fr 1:8 \fr*\ft Or \+it concerning you all, that...\+it*\ft*\f*for you all, because your faith is being proclaimed throughout the world.
\v 9 For God, whom I serve in my spirit in the \it preaching of the\it* gospel of His Son, is my witness \it as to\it* how unceasingly I make mention of you,
\v 10 always in my prayers requesting if perhaps now, at last by the will of God, I will succeed in coming to you.
\v 11 For I long to see you so that I may impart some spiritual gift to you, that you may be \f 1 \fr 1:11 \fr*\ft Or \+it strengthened\+it*\ft*\f*established;
\v 12 that is, that I may be encouraged together with you \it while\it* among you, each of us by the other’s faith, both yours and mine.
\v 13 I do not want you to be unaware, brothers \it and sisters,\it* that often I have planned to come to you (and have been prevented so far) so that I may obtain some fruit among you also just as among the rest of the Gentiles.
\v 14 I am \f 1 \fr 1:14 \fr*\ft Lit \+it debtor\+it*\ft*\f*under obligation both to Greeks and to the \f 2 \fr 1:14 \fr*\ft I.e., non-Hellenes\ft*\f*uncultured, both to the wise and to the foolish.
\v 15 So, for my part, I am eager to preach the gospel to you also who are in Rome.
\v 16 For I am not ashamed of the gospel, for it is the power of God for salvation to everyone who believes, to the Jew first and also to the Greek.
\v 17 For in it \it the\it* righteousness of God is revealed \f 1 \fr 1:17 \fr*\ft Or \+it by\+it*\ft*\f*from faith to faith; as it is written: “\f 2 \fr 1:17 \fr*\ft Or \+it But the one who is righteous by faith shall live\+it*\ft*\f*B\sc ut the righteous \+it one\+it* will live by faith\sc*.”
\v 18 For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of people who suppress the truth \f 1 \fr 1:18 \fr*\ft Or \+it by\+it*\ft*\f*in unrighteousness,
\v 19 because that which is known about God is evident \f 1 \fr 1:19 \fr*\ft Or \+it among\+it*\ft*\f*within them; for God made it evident to them.
\v 20 For since the creation of the world His invisible \it attributes, that is,\it* His eternal power and divine nature, have been clearly perceived, being understood by what has been made, so that they are without excuse.
\v 21 For even though they knew God, they did not \f 1 \fr 1:21 \fr*\ft Lit \+it glorify\+it*\ft*\f*honor Him as God or give thanks, but they became futile in their reasonings, and their senseless hearts were darkened.
\v 22 Claiming to be wise, they became fools,
\v 23 and they exchanged the glory of the incorruptible God for an image in the form of corruptible mankind, of birds, four-footed animals, and \f 1 \fr 1:23 \fr*\ft Or \+it reptiles\+it*\ft*\f*crawling creatures.
\v 24 Therefore God gave them up to vile impurity in the lusts of their hearts, so that their bodies would be dishonored among them.
\v 25 For they exchanged the truth of God for \f 1 \fr 1:25 \fr*\ft Lit \+it the lie\+it*\ft*\f*falsehood, and worshiped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is blessed \f 2 \fr 1:25 \fr*\ft Lit \+it unto the ages\+it*\ft*\f*forever. Amen.
\v 26 For this reason God gave them over to degrading passions; for their women exchanged natural relations for that which is contrary to nature,
\v 27 and likewise the men, too, abandoned natural relations \f 1 \fr 1:27 \fr*\ft Lit \+it of the female\+it*\ft*\f*with women and burned in their desire toward one another, males with males committing \f 2 \fr 1:27 \fr*\ft Lit \+it shamelessness\+it*\ft*\f*shameful acts and receiving in \f 3 \fr 1:27 \fr*\ft Lit \+it themselves\+it*\ft*\f*their own persons the due penalty of their error.
\v 28 And just as they did not see fit \f 1 \fr 1:28 \fr*\ft Lit \+it to have God in knowledge\+it*\ft*\f*to acknowledge God, God gave them up to a depraved mind, to do those things that are not proper,
\v 29 \it people\it* having been filled with all unrighteousness, wickedness, greed, \it and\it* evil; full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, \it and\it* malice; \it they are\it* gossips,
\v 30 slanderers, \f 1 \fr 1:30 \fr*\ft Or \+it hateful to God\+it*\ft*\f*haters of God, insolent, arrogant, boastful, inventors of evil, disobedient to parents,
\v 31 without understanding, untrustworthy, unfeeling, \it and\it* unmerciful;
\v 32 and although they know the ordinance of God, that those who practice such things are worthy of death, they not only do the same, but also approve of those who practice them.
\c 2
\v 1 Therefore you have no excuse, \f 1 \fr 2:1 \fr*\ft Lit \+it O\+it*\ft*\f*you \it foolish\it* person, everyone \it of you\it* who passes judgment; for \f 2 \fr 2:1 \fr*\ft Or \+it when you judge\+it*\ft*\f*in that \it matter in\it* which you judge someone else, you condemn yourself; for you who judge practice the same things.
\v 2 And we know that the judgment of God \f 1 \fr 2:2 \fr*\ft Lit \+it is according to truth against\+it*\ft*\f*rightly falls upon those who practice such things.
\v 3 But do you suppose this, \f 1 \fr 2:3 \fr*\ft Lit \+it O\+it*\ft*\f*you \it foolish\it* person who passes judgment on those who practice such things, and \it yet\it* does them \it as well,\it* that you will escape the judgment of God?
\v 4 Or do you think lightly of the riches of His kindness and \f 1 \fr 2:4 \fr*\ft I.e., from inflicting punishment\ft*\f*restraint and patience, not knowing that the kindness of God leads you to repentance?
\v 5 But \f 1 \fr 2:5 \fr*\ft Or \+it in accordance with\+it*\ft*\f*because of your stubbornness and unrepentant heart you are storing up wrath for yourself on the day of wrath and revelation of the righteous judgment of God,
\v 6 who \sc will repay each person according to his deeds\sc*:
\v 7 to those who by perseverance in doing good seek glory, honor, and immortality, \it He will give\it* eternal life;
\v 8 but to those who are self-serving and do not obey the truth, but obey unrighteousness, \it He will give\it* wrath and indignation.
\v 9 \it There will be\it* tribulation and distress \f 1 \fr 2:9 \fr*\ft Lit \+it upon\+it*\ft*\f*for every soul of mankind who does evil, \f 2 \fr 2:9 \fr*\ft Lit \+it of the\+it*\ft*\f*for the Jew first and also \f 3 \fr 2:9 \fr*\ft Lit \+it of the\+it*\ft*\f*for the Greek,
\v 10 but glory, honor, and peace to everyone who does what is good, to the Jew first and also to the Greek.
\v 11 For there is no partiality with God.
